# Accepted risks for the Trivy CRITICAL gate in .github/workflows/ci-cd.yml.
# Each entry needs a reason and an expiry; after the date the entry is ignored by Trivy and the
# gate fails again, which forces a re-review instead of letting an exception live forever.

# spring-webmvc 6.2.19 (managed by Spring Boot 3.5.16, the newest 3.5.x/6.2.x).
# Fixed ONLY in Spring Framework 7.0.9 (Spring Boot 4); no 6.2.x patch exists.
#  - CVE-2026-47884: RCE/SSRF via XsltView with a "/**" mapping and no explicit view name.
#  - CVE-2026-47890: stream corruption for Server-Sent Events with view fragments.
# Not reachable here: eventstracker uses no XsltView/XSLT, no SSE endpoints, and no catch-all
# "/**" mapping (checked 2026-10-19). Real fix: migrate to Spring Boot 4 (runs-app is on 4.0.1).
# Accepted by: sathishjayapal on 2026-10-19. Review by the expiry below.
CVE-2026-47884 exp:2027-01-31
CVE-2026-47890 exp:2027-01-31
